commit b699cf0f42f0d6b0ec92c47489a6a1df7e112d90
Author: Christian Brauner <brauner@kernel.org>
Date:   Wed Nov 18 16:09:03 2026 +0100

    fixup! vfs: prepare vfs_creat|mkdir_no_perm for reuse in lookup_open()

    Keep the "no ->create()/->mkdir()" checks in vfs_create() and
    vfs_mkdir() in front of the LSM hooks. Otherwise we call into the LSM
    for an operation the filesystem doesn't implement and SELinux can end
    up auditing a denial for it. vfs_mknod(), vfs_symlink(), vfs_link(),
    vfs_rmdir() and vfs_unlink() all check for the operation first too.
    The copies in the helpers are still needed for lookup_open().

    Signed-off-by: Christian Brauner (Amutable) <brauner@kernel.org>

